# Per-test plusargs for exc_irq_ccr_settle.
#
# Inject a level-1 IRQ at cycle 83.  This is timing-tuned so the IRQ
# arms at the CMP -> BCS boundary and take_irq_fire_q samples the CCR
# in the CMP's commit-settle window.  On a pre-fix build the race
# window is +ipl cycles 82..84 (verified by sweep); 83 is the centre.
#
# If front-end latency shifts and the IRQ stops landing on that
# boundary the test will false-PASS — re-tune by sweeping +ipl and
# finding the cycle that FAILs on a build without the
# ccr_settle_in_flight gate.  The +irq_at_cycle ROM repro
# (docs / task #41) is the authoritative cross-check.
#
# +ipl=cycle:level — single-shot IPL pulse, cleared on cpu_ipl_ack.
+ipl=83:1
